            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention relates to a cooking vessel including a bottomed cylindrical body having an upper opening; and a pair of handles provided on the body, wherein each of the handles has a gripping member that is sloped in a lateral view with respect to an upper rim section of the body, allowing users to turn the vessel while effortlessly maintaining a natural posture.</p>
